# @see R-030 (Design Patterns vs Native Platform Features)
id: PATTERN-007
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 4
action: advisory
title: Repository wrapper around ORM that already provides repositories
category: quality
severity: info
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .java .kt .cs .py .rb
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: class\s+\w+Repository\s.*extends\s+(Repository|BaseRepository|TypeOrmRepository)
    message: "Custom repository extending ORM Repository — TypeORM/MikroORM already provide repository methods. Only add a wrapper if you have custom query logic"
  - regex: extends\s+JpaRepository|extends\s+CrudRepository
    message: "Spring Data JPA repository — Spring Data already generates implementations. Custom methods use @Query, no wrapper class needed"
  - regex: class\s+\w+Repository.*\.(find|save|delete|create|update)\s*\(
    message: "Repository with pass-through CRUD methods — if just delegating to ORM, the wrapper adds no value. Use the ORM directly or add only custom queries"
fix: Remove the repository wrapper if it only delegates to ORM methods. Spring Data, TypeORM, Prisma, Eloquent, and ActiveRecord already implement the Repository pattern. Add a custom repository only for complex query logic.
